If, on account of the temporary absence or disability of the city manager, it should be necessary in the judgment of the mayor and city council members to designate some person to serve as acting city manager during the temporary absence or disability of the city manager, the mayor and city council may execute one of the following options:
(1) The mayor may assume the responsibilities of the duties of the city manager until the city manager returns to his or her office;
(2) The mayor and city council may appoint the city clerk to assume the responsibilities and duties of the city manager;
(3) The mayor and city council may appoint any qualified person to temporarily serve as city manager and fix his or her compensation.

